# Projections: the forms of projecting activation rows by weights, written
# once per backend and taken by an entry's native declaration with one
# `project` line (`seismic/lang/src/projection.rs`). The formals: M
# activation rows, K columns, N rows of each weight, WEIGHTS the weights one
# activation row serves (`paired`: two, a gate and an up weight whose
# products one epilogue combines; `single`: one; `segmented`: one to four,
# each of its own N rows, possibly none, projecting the rows into its own
# columns, one served a row), W a weight in a quantifier or an `each W:`
# block, and G the groups of the weights' rows (1 unless the entry names
# them): group g projects its own K columns of the rows by its own N weight
# rows into its own N columns.

# Second-level weight scales (every entry reading packed weights): one
# `<weight>_scale` port per weight, after every other argument, in weight
# order, `[S] f32` per tensor (or `[S, E] f32` per expert in the routed
# entries). S = 1 carries the scale (NVFP4 `.scale`), applied to that
# projection's F32 accumulator before anything else (`scale_rows`); S = 0 is
# no scale, and the natives compile the scaling out. S is static on every
# backend.

# Packing bounds (the entries with a token-packing form: `dense_expand`,
# `dense_output`, `project_rows`, `attention_output`, `attention_project`,
# `gated_delta_project`): one `<weight>_bound` port per packed weight, after
# the scales, `[B] f32`. B = K / n carries the weight's packing bound
# (`packing_bound`, `WeightPlan::bound`): per run of the n columns that share
# a scale, the largest squared l2 norm of a row's codes minus their centre,
# over the tensor's rows, which certifies a packed operand's gain for this
# tensor rather than for every row of the format. B = 0 is no bound. No
# result depends on it but a packed form's, whose error it lowers; B is
# static on every backend. On Metal a bound offers the packed form's wider
# residue (`RESIDUE` 2: one more bit of top sum, half the top token's step),
# which applies only to weights whose packed entries are 8 bits
# (`forms::metal_packing`): the declarations admit it only for a bounded
# weight whose codes take it (`form(W, PACK_RESIDUE)`).

# Metal: the K1 projection library (`metal/lib/projection/`, the form bodies
# in `operator.h`). Output rows up to VERIFY_ROWS run the GEMV launch
# (SIMDGROUPS x ROWS lane groups of LANES lanes per threadgroup, each owning
# weight rows; LANES sets the reduction order, so it is arithmetic; TILED = 1
# is the form over `rows32` weights: the same weight rows per threadgroup, a
# thread owning one of them and a simdgroup's lanes consecutive rows of a
# tile, with a summation order of its own, `gemv_tile_row`; TILED = 2 is the
# row mapping walked by packet class over `rows32` weights, `gemv_classes`,
# with the row mapping's results under the same LANES). An entry launches it
# three times, `gemv` for one row, `gemv_pair` for two and `gemv_rows` for
# three rows up to VERIFY_ROWS, each with its own threadgroup mapping and each
# instantiating only the row bounds it runs: the fastest mapping of one row
# is not that of several. A row's result is the same in all three only under
# the same LANES and TILED, so both are the projection's settings, one value
# the three launches read: a row's bits never depend on how many rows its
# call carries up to VERIFY_ROWS, the rows a draft verification carries: the
# batched form below starts above them.
# PACKED_ROWS = N (2 or 3, at most the weight's `form(W, PACK_LANES)`)
# takes 2..VERIFY_ROWS rows by the packed-rows GEMV instead (`gemv_packed`,
# over weights the packed GEMM admits without residue bits; as PACK, a
# device with tensor operations runs the GEMV's body in its place): N rows as
# one F32 operand of packed integer codes, so a chain's FMA carries N rows'
# products, with the GEMV's row mapping; it stages its own operand, so STAGE
# is off. A row's
# result then depends on the rows packed with it, so the launch is not alike
# the GEMV; the precision system admits the form per unit.
# The entry's prologue forms the GEMV's rows in-threadgroup, so a decode
# projection is one launch; in larger classes the entry's own pre-pass first
# writes its rows to scratch.
# VERIFY_ROWS + 1..16 rows the batched launch on the matrix units (BATCH_SIMDGROUPS
# x BATCH_ROWS blocks of 8 weight rows, F32 operands, a different summation
# order, so its start above VERIFY_ROWS matters too; with MATRIX = 1, which the
# projection admits only over weights with a matrix form (`form(W, MATRIX)`,
# which `forms::metal_matrix` admits: integer lane codes under factors per
# 256 columns, or direct scales per 32), the launch takes the matrix GEMV
# instead, `gemv_matrix`: the weights' integer codes as the left fragment
# (whole 256-column blocks for the codes and runs products, which sum a
# block's factors once and would drop a partial one; whole 32-column groups
# for the symmetric product),
# BATCH_PARTS simdgroups sharing a fragment's eight weight rows, a summation
# order of its own; BATCH_ROWS is the batched rows' and BATCH_PARTS the
# matrix GEMV's, each held at its default in the other form; a segmented
# projection takes it for the segments it serves, over the rows its entry
# stages for it, and the batched rows (BATCH_ROWS) for the others, its other
# form normalizing in-threadgroup as the GEMV does);
# 17..64 rows the GEMM at the fixed small-row geometry
# (`gemm_small`: 32 x 64 tiles, 4-way split-K where the projection is
# single) where SMALL is 1, else the tuned GEMM below; larger classes the GEMM over tuned
# TILE_M x TILE_N tiles
# (activations staged as stored, weights decoded to half once per tile), with
# SPLIT-way split-K where the projection is single (a paired epilogue reads
# whole sums).
# TALL selects the tall GEMM past 64 rows (`gemm_tall`): TALL_M rows by 32
# weight rows per threadgroup, STAGERS staging simdgroups decoding the
# weights once for all its rows, TALL_K columns per stage, and the
# activations read from device memory. On simdgroup matrices they are read in
# fragment order: a paired entry's pre-pass writes that order, and a single
# projection first reorders its rows into `fragments` (a second copy of them,
# in whole 64-row tiles). The form needs K a multiple of 128 and has no
# split-K; its staged producer reads every weight, dense ones included
# (`forms` admits it for all), and where it is admitted it is the default,
# with the same results as the tiles above.
# PACK selects the token-packing GEMM past 64 rows (`gemm_packed`, over the
# weights `forms::metal_packing` admits, integer lane codes not scaled by a
# power of two of their own whose coefficients fold per run of a 32-column
# block, on a device without tensor operations, and where paired a gate and
# an up weight one operand serves, whose runs and entry widths agree:
# `form(W, PACK)` of each weight, and the same `PACK_FOLDS` and
# `PACK_RESIDUE`); devices with tensor operations run the staged tile, with
# its results, in the `unpacked` launch, and each launch of the other path
# returns at once): the activations become integer codes per (row, 32 columns)
# and two rows share one F32 matrix operand element against the weights'
# stored codes, so a row's result depends on the row it is packed with
# (`int8_token_packing`). Three rows an element, which narrow codes have room
# for, err above admission at every format that admits them (tuner ratio 10-40
# BF16 steps against alpha 8 on q2k, q2g64, q2g256, q1g128 and iq1s at 4096 x
# 4096, 512 rows: the bottom lane's codes are about 5 bits, about 6% relative
# error), so the form packs two. A simdgroup multiplies PACK_TOKENS operand
# fragments (16 rows each) by 8 / PACK_TOKENS weight fragments (8 weight rows
# each), four of them a threadgroup (independent tiles; a gate and an up
# simdgroup pair where paired); WEIGHTS_AHEAD loads a block's weight words one
# block ahead (the best of both differs by device and shape). The `where`
# holds the form's launch parameters at their defaults outside the form, and
# the staged and tall tiles' inside it, where they are not launched, so the
# form's configurations do not multiply another's. Its scratch is transient,
# per call: the packed operand (`packed`, 2 bytes per padded row and column,
# plus one step read ahead), the rows' scales and code sums, or for 8-bit
# entries (`PACK_RESIDUE`) the rows' scales and the RESIDUE low bit planes of
# their codes (`token_factors`, 4 bytes per padded row and 32 columns, 8 with
# two planes or with each run's code sums, `PACK_SUMS`; RESIDUE 2 takes a
# packing bound, `bound(W)`, and applies only to weights whose packed entries
# are 8 bits) and each weight's block scales and biases (`<stem>_factors`, 4
# bytes per weight row and 32 columns, 8 with each run's min term), both held
# over one power of two per row (`token_scales`, `<stem>_scales`, 4 bytes a
# row; a weight tile's 32 rows share theirs) so that the F16 fold cannot
# overflow. Quantized operands pad the rows to TOKENS, 64 where paired (a tile
# serves both weights) and 128 where single; packed ones likewise, one operand
# tile of 64 rows where paired and two where single (`packing_padded`).
# STAGE stages the GEMV launches' row-mapping activations as F32,
# rounded to A first, so the same values: twice the threadgroup bytes, and no
# split of A at every step of every weight row. It pays where the decode
# bounds the GEMV and costs where memory does, so it is tuned. It is declared
# only where the row mapping reads it, a parted entry's partial GEMV among
# them: not over the row tiles or the class walk (TILED 0), and not over a
# plane set, whose entries share one declaration while the exact view's
# recipe stages its own rows and cannot hold them as F32 at 8 rows (a lane
# stride of 32 packets each). Its halved chunk holds no packet a lane at
# LANES 32 over 8 rows (LANES < 32).
# INT8 selects the int8 GEMM past 64 rows over the weights `form(W, INT8)`
# admits: the rows quantized per (row, 32 columns), each weight's block
# coefficients and biases, then the int8 tiles.
# Segmented: each launch's threadgroups take the segments in turn, each its
# own (`tiles(W, ..)`); PACK packs the segments whose rows are whole 32-row
# tiles and whose weights the one operand serves, into one factor table of
# every segment's rows (`sum(W, N)`), and the staged 64 x 64 tiles
# (`unpacked`) run the others; an entry's results may be zeros for a call
# (each form's threadgroups of the segment store them).
# Parts (`parts P`, segmented): the GEMVs split K by part, P times the
# tiles, each threadgroup a part's row tile over that part's own rows
# (`PROJECTION_SEGMENTED_PARTS_GEMV`), into F32 `partials`; the last of a
# row tile's P threadgroups to arrive (`arrivals`, a counter a row tile)
# adds them in part order. The batched launch and the tuned GEMM read whole
# rows; no other form reads parts (TALL, PACK, MATRIX, SMALL and TILED are 0
# for a parted entry).
# Groups: the GEMVs, the batched launch, the reductions, the relayout and
# the tall GEMM run group g at grid z, the GEMMs at z = g * split + part, each
# over its own G-th of the split partials and of the tall form's fragments;
# the forms that stage or pack whole rows or weights (INT8, PACK, the matrix
# GEMV, NVFP4 operands) run only G = 1.
# A plane set (`PLANES`, a progressive head's planes; `readout.seismic`)
# takes the GEMVs, the batched rows and the staged tiles over the packets of
# its view: a view whose packets name a recipe (`gemv_recipe`, the exact
# view) is projected at the GEMV's rows by that recipe, which the exact
# level's gather shares, so the two agree bit for bit. Every other form,
# with its scratch, is gated off a plane set (TALL, SMALL, MATRIX and TILED
# are 0 for one, and its GEMM does not split).
# Admission: each form's `where` states what it needs once, of the weights
# (`form(W, ..)`) and of the entry's facts (`GATHERED`, `PLANES`, `PARTED`:
# the forms that stage or code whole weight rows in storage order, TALL and
# MATRIX with INT8 and PACK, serve no gathered rows). An entry's range of a
# form is what those lines leave of it; no entry restates a form.
projection dense for metal:
    let ORDERED_ANY = min(1, sum(W, ORDERED))
    let ORDERED_ALL = sum(W, ORDERED) / WEIGHTS
    let ORDERED_GEMV_SHARED = 8192
    let MIXED_GEMV_SHARED = min(ceil_div(K, 32) * (min(M, 2) + 2 * min(M / 3, 1) + 4 * min(M / 5, 1)), 448) * 64
    let TOKENS = 128 / SERVED
    let SPLITS = 1 for paired | segmented
    let SPLITS = SPLIT for single
    let SMALL_SPLITS = 1 for paired | segmented
    let SMALL_SPLITS = 4 for single
    let INT8 = 0 for segmented
    let PACKED_ROWS = 0 for paired | segmented
    params (arithmetic SPLIT in [1, 2, 4] default 1 for single,
        SIMDGROUPS in [8, 16, 4, 2] default 8 for ordered, ROWS in [1, 2, 4] default 1 for ordered,
        form TALL in [1, 0] default (1 - ORDERED_ANY),
        arithmetic form INT8 in [0, 1] default 0 for paired | single, arithmetic form PACK in [0, 1] default 0, arithmetic form RESIDUE in [1, 2] default 1,
        arithmetic form MATRIX in [1, 0] default (1 - ORDERED_ANY),
        arithmetic form SMALL in [1, 0] default (1 - ORDERED_ANY),
        arithmetic LANES in [16, 32, 8] default (16 + 16 * ORDERED_ANY), arithmetic form TILED in [0, 1, 2] default 0,
        form STAGE in [0, 1] default 0,
        arithmetic form PACKED_ROWS in [0, 2, 3] default 0 for single)
    where dense_bytes(A) == 2
    where (ORDERED_ANY == 0 or (TALL == 0 and PACK == 0 and RESIDUE == 1 and MATRIX == 0 and SMALL == 0 and LANES != 8 and TILED == 0))
    where (ORDERED_ANY == 0 or SPLIT == 1) for single
    where (ORDERED_ANY == 0 or INT8 == 0) for paired | single
    where (ORDERED_ALL == 0 or ROWS == 1) for ordered
    where (ORDERED_ALL == 0 or LANES == 32)
    where (TILED == 0 or (PLANES == 0 and PARTED == 0))
    where (STAGE == 0 or PLANES == 0)
    where (STAGE == 0 or (TILED == 0 and LANES < 32))
    where (TALL == 0 or (GATHERED == 0 and PLANES == 0 and PARTED == 0 and SPLITS == 1 and K % 128 == 0))
    where (SMALL == 0 or (PLANES == 0 and PARTED == 0))
    where (SPLIT == 1 or PLANES == 0) for single
    where (INT8 == 0 or (GATHERED == 0 and TALL == 1 and K % 512 == 0 and N % (64 / WEIGHTS) == 0 and each(W, form(W, INT8) == 1) and agree(W, form(W, INT8_INTERLEAVED)))) for paired | single
    where (INT8 == 1 or INT8_TILE == 128) for single
    where (PACK == 0 or (GATHERED == 0 and TALL == 1 and INT8 == 0 and K % 256 == 0 and K < 1048576 and N % (64 / WEIGHTS) == 0 and each(W, form(W, PACK) == 1) and agree(W, form(W, PACK_FOLDS)) and agree(W, form(W, PACK_RESIDUE)) and agree(W, form(W, PACK_SUMS)))) for paired | single
    where (PACK == 0 or (PARTED == 0 and TALL == 1 and K % 256 == 0 and K < 1048576 and SERVED == 1 and any(W, N > 0 and N % 32 == 0 and form(W, PACK) == 1))) for segmented
    where (PACK == 1 or (PACK_TOKENS == 4 and WEIGHTS_AHEAD == 0))
    where (PACK == 0 or (TILE_M == 64 and TILE_N == 64))
    where (PACK == 0 or (TALL_M == 128 and TALL_K == 64 and STAGERS == 2))
    where (RESIDUE == 1 or (PACK == 1 and any(W, bound(W) > 0 and form(W, PACK_RESIDUE) == 1)))
    where (G == 1 or (INT8 == 0 and PACK == 0 and MATRIX == 0 and each(W, operands(W) == 0)))
    where (PACKED_ROWS == 0 or (ORDERED_ANY == 0 and TILED == 0 and STAGE == 0 and G == 1 and GATHERED == 0 and PLANES == 0 and PARTED == 0 and each(W, operands(W) == 0 and form(W, PACK) == 1 and form(W, PACK_RESIDUE) == 0 and form(W, PACK_LANES) >= PACKED_ROWS))) for single
    where (MATRIX == 0 or (GATHERED == 0 and each(W, form(W, MATRIX) == 1 and (K % 256 == 0 or (form(W, MATRIX_SYMMETRIC) == 1 and K % 32 == 0))))) for paired | single
    where (MATRIX == 0 or (PARTED == 0 and any(W, N > 0 and form(W, MATRIX) == 1 and (K % 256 == 0 or (form(W, MATRIX_SYMMETRIC) == 1 and K % 32 == 0))))) for segmented
    where (MATRIX == 1 or BATCH_PARTS == 2)
    where (MATRIX == 0 or BATCH_ROWS == 2) for paired | single
    scratch staged bytes (M * K * 2) when ORDERED_ALL == 1 and PUBLISHED == 0 and M > VERIFY_ROWS for rms
    scratch partials bytes (SPLIT * G * M * N * 4) when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 16 and (M > 64 or SMALL == 0) and SPLIT > 1 and PLANES == 0 for single
    scratch partials bytes (M * P * sum(W, N) * 4) when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M <= VERIFY_ROWS and PARTED == 1 for segmented
    scratch arrivals bytes (sum(W, N) * 4) sync when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M <= VERIFY_ROWS and PARTED == 1 for segmented
    scratch small_partials bytes (4 * G * M * N * 4) when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 16 and M <= 64 and SMALL == 1 and PLANES == 0 for single
    scratch fragments bytes (G * ceil_div(M, 64) * 64 * K * 2) when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 64 and TALL == 1 and INT8 == 0 and PACK == 0 and PLANES == 0 for single
    scratch packed bytes (ceil_div(M, TOKENS) * TOKENS * K * 2 + 1024) when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 64 and PACK == 1 and PLANES == 0
    scratch token_factors bytes (ceil_div(M, TOKENS) * TOKENS * (K / 32) * 4 * max(RESIDUE, 1 + most(W, form(W, PACK_SUMS)))) when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 64 and PACK == 1 and PLANES == 0
    each W:
        scratch factors bytes (N * (K / 32) * 4 * (1 + form(W, PACK_SUMS))) when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 64 and PACK == 1 and PLANES == 0 for paired | single
    scratch factors bytes (sum(W, N) * (K / 32) * 4 * (1 + most(W, form(W, PACK_SUMS)))) when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 64 and PACK == 1 for segmented
    scratch token_scales bytes (ceil_div(M, TOKENS) * TOKENS * 4) when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 64 and PACK == 1 and PLANES == 0
    each W:
        scratch scales bytes (N * 4) when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 64 and PACK == 1 and PLANES == 0 for paired | single
    scratch scales bytes (sum(W, N) * 4) when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 64 and PACK == 1 for segmented
    scratch quantized bytes (ceil_div(M, TOKENS) * TOKENS * K) when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 64 and INT8 == 1 and PLANES == 0 for paired | single
    scratch row_scales bytes (ceil_div(M, TOKENS) * TOKENS * (K / 32) * 2) when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 64 and INT8 == 1 and PLANES == 0 for paired | single
    scratch block_sums bytes (ceil_div(M, TOKENS) * TOKENS * ceil_div(K, 1024) * 32 * 2) when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 64 and INT8 == 1 and PLANES == 0 for paired | single
    each W:
        scratch coefficients bytes (N * (K / 32) * 4) when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 64 and INT8 == 1 and PLANES == 0 for paired | single
        scratch biases bytes (ceil_div(N, 32) * 32 * ceil_div(K, 1024) * 32 * 2) when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 64 and INT8 == 1 and PLANES == 0 for paired | single
    launch ordered_stage for rms when ORDERED_ALL == 1 and M > VERIFY_ROWS:
        staging
        threadgroups (M, 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
    launch ordered_gemv when ORDERED_ALL == 1 and M <= VERIFY_ROWS:
        threadgroups (tiles(W, ceil_div(N, SIMDGROUPS * 4)), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (SIMDGROUPS * 32, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (ORDERED_GEMV_SHARED)
    launch ordered_gemv1 for segmented when ORDERED_ANY == 1 and ORDERED_ALL == 0 and M <= 1:
        threadgroups (tiles(W, ORDERED * ceil_div(N, min(SIMDGROUPS, 2) * 4) + (1 - ORDERED) * ceil_div(N, SIMDGROUPS * ROWS * 32 / LANES)), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (SIMDGROUPS * 32, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (max(1024, MIXED_GEMV_SHARED))
    launch ordered_gemv2 for segmented when ORDERED_ANY == 1 and ORDERED_ALL == 0 and M == 2:
        alike (ordered_gemv1)
        threadgroups (tiles(W, ORDERED * ceil_div(N, SIMDGROUPS * 2) + (1 - ORDERED) * ceil_div(N, SIMDGROUPS * ROWS * 32 / LANES)), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (SIMDGROUPS * 32, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (max(1536, MIXED_GEMV_SHARED))
    launch ordered_gemv4 for segmented when ORDERED_ANY == 1 and ORDERED_ALL == 0 and M >= 3 and M <= 4:
        alike (ordered_gemv1)
        threadgroups (tiles(W, ORDERED * ceil_div(N, SIMDGROUPS) + (1 - ORDERED) * ceil_div(N, SIMDGROUPS * ROWS * 32 / LANES)), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (SIMDGROUPS * 32, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (max(2560, MIXED_GEMV_SHARED))
    launch ordered_gemv8 for segmented when ORDERED_ANY == 1 and ORDERED_ALL == 0 and M >= 5 and M <= VERIFY_ROWS:
        alike (ordered_gemv1)
        threadgroups (tiles(W, ORDERED * ceil_div(N, SIMDGROUPS) + (1 - ORDERED) * ceil_div(N, SIMDGROUPS * ROWS * 32 / LANES)), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (SIMDGROUPS * 32, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (max(4608, MIXED_GEMV_SHARED))
    launch ordered_gemm when ORDERED_ALL == 1 and M > VERIFY_ROWS:
        threadgroups (tiles(W, ceil_div(N, 32)), ceil_div(M, 32), G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (8192)
    launch gemv when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M < 2:
        params (SIMDGROUPS in [16, 8, 4, 2, 32] default 16, ROWS in [1, 2, 4] default 1)
        threadgroups (P * tiles(W, ceil_div(N, SIMDGROUPS * ROWS * 32 / LANES)), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (SIMDGROUPS * 32, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (max(min(ceil_div(K / P, 32) * (min(M, 2) + 2 * min(M / 3, 1) + 4 * min(M / 5, 1)), 448 / (1 + STAGE)) * 64 * (1 + STAGE), TILED * SIMDGROUPS * (128 * SERVED)))
    launch batch when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > VERIFY_ROWS and M <= 16:
        params (BATCH_SIMDGROUPS in [8, 4, 16, 32] default 8, BATCH_ROWS in [2, 1, 4] default 2,
            arithmetic BATCH_PARTS in [2, 4, 1] default 2)
        reads (MATRIX)
        threadgroups (tiles(W, MATRIX * ceil_div(ceil_div(N, 8) * BATCH_PARTS, BATCH_SIMDGROUPS)
            + (1 - MATRIX) * ceil_div(N, BATCH_SIMDGROUPS * BATCH_ROWS * 8)), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (BATCH_SIMDGROUPS * 32, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (max(16640, MATRIX * min((BATCH_SIMDGROUPS * 256 + ceil_div(K, 32) * 32) * ceil_div(M, 8), 28672)))
    launch gemm_small when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 16 and M <= 64 and SMALL == 1 and PLANES == 0:
        threadgroups (tiles(W, ceil_div(N, 64 / SERVED)), ceil_div(M, 32), SMALL_SPLITS * G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (128, 1, 1)
    launch reduce_small for single when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 16 and M <= 64 and SMALL == 1 and PLANES == 0:
        threadgroups (ceil_div(M * N, 256), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
    launch gemm when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 16 and (M > 64 or SMALL == 0) and (M <= 64 or TALL == 0):
        params (TILE_M in [64, 128, 32] default 64, TILE_N in [64, 128] default 64)
        threadgroups (tiles(W, ceil_div(N, TILE_N / SERVED)), ceil_div(M, TILE_M), SPLITS * G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (max(TILE_M, 64) * TILE_N / 32, 1, 1)
    launch reduce for single when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 16 and (M > 64 or SMALL == 0) and SPLIT > 1 and PLANES == 0:
        threadgroups (ceil_div(M * N, 256), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
    launch relayout for single when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 64 and TALL == 1 and INT8 == 0 and PACK == 0 and PLANES == 0:
        threadgroups (ceil_div(ceil_div(M, 64) * K, 256), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
    launch tall when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 64 and TALL == 1 and INT8 == 0 and PACK == 0 and PLANES == 0:
        params (TALL_M in [128, 256, 512] default 128, TALL_K in [64, 128] default 64, STAGERS in [2, 1] default 2)
        threadgroups (tiles(W, ceil_div(N, 32 / SERVED)), ceil_div(M, TALL_M), G)
        threads_per_threadgroup ((TALL_M / 32 + STAGERS) * 32, 1, 1)
    launch quantize for paired | single when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 64 and INT8 == 1 and PLANES == 0:
        threadgroups (ceil_div(M, TOKENS) * TOKENS, 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
    launch coefficients for paired | single when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 64 and INT8 == 1 and PLANES == 0:
        threadgroups (ceil_div(N * (K / 256), 1024), 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
    launch int8 for paired when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 64 and INT8 == 1 and PLANES == 0:
        threadgroups (ceil_div(N, 32), ceil_div(M, 64), 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (128, 1, 1)
    launch int8 for single when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 64 and INT8 == 1 and PLANES == 0:
        params (INT8_TILE in [128, 64] default 128)
        threadgroups (ceil_div(M, INT8_TILE), (INT8_TILE / 128) * ceil_div(N, 32) + (1 - INT8_TILE / 128) * ceil_div(N, 64), 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (128, 1, 1)
    launch gemv_rows when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and PACKED_ROWS == 0 and M >= 3 and M <= VERIFY_ROWS:
        params (SIMDGROUPS in [8, 16, 4, 2, 32] default 8, ROWS in [1, 2, 4] default 1 for paired | segmented, ROWS in [2, 1, 4] default 2 for single)
        alike (gemv)
        threadgroups (P * tiles(W, ceil_div(N, SIMDGROUPS * ROWS * 32 / LANES)), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (SIMDGROUPS * 32, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (max(min(ceil_div(K / P, 32) * (min(M, 2) + 2 * min(M / 3, 1) + 4 * min(M / 5, 1)), 448 / (1 + STAGE)) * 64 * (1 + STAGE), TILED * SIMDGROUPS * (128 * SERVED)))
    launch gemv_packed for single when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and PACKED_ROWS > 0 and PLANES == 0 and M >= 2 and M <= VERIFY_ROWS:
        params (SIMDGROUPS in [8, 16, 4, 2, 32] default 8, ROWS in [2, 1, 4] default 2)
        threadgroups (tiles(W, ceil_div(N, SIMDGROUPS * ROWS * 32 / LANES)), 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (SIMDGROUPS * 32, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (min(ceil_div(K, 32) * (128 * ceil_div(min(M, 2) + 2 * min(M / 3, 1) + 4 * min(M / 5, 1), PACKED_ROWS) + 16 * (min(M, 2) + 2 * min(M / 3, 1) + 4 * min(M / 5, 1))), 28672))
    launch gemv_pair when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and PACKED_ROWS == 0 and M == 2:
        params (SIMDGROUPS in [8, 16, 4, 2, 32] default 8, ROWS in [1, 2, 4] default 1 for paired | segmented, ROWS in [2, 1, 4] default 2 for single)
        alike (gemv)
        threadgroups (P * tiles(W, ceil_div(N, SIMDGROUPS * ROWS * 32 / LANES)), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (SIMDGROUPS * 32, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (max(min(ceil_div(K / P, 32) * (min(M, 2) + 2 * min(M / 3, 1) + 4 * min(M / 5, 1)), 448 / (1 + STAGE)) * 64 * (1 + STAGE), TILED * SIMDGROUPS * (128 * SERVED)))
    launch pack when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 64 and PACK == 1 and PLANES == 0:
        reads (RESIDUE)
        threadgroups (ceil_div(M, TOKENS) * (TOKENS / 4), 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
    launch pack_coefficients for paired | single when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 64 and PACK == 1 and PLANES == 0:
        threadgroups (N / 32, 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
    launch pack_coefficients for segmented when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 64 and PACK == 1:
        threadgroups (sum(W, N), 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (32, 1, 1)
    launch packed when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 64 and PACK == 1 and PLANES == 0:
        params (PACK_TOKENS in [4, 2] default 4, WEIGHTS_AHEAD in [0, 1] default 0)
        reads (RESIDUE)
        threadgroups (tiles(W, ceil_div(M, TOKENS) * (N / 32)), 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (128, 1, 1)
    launch unpacked when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 64 and PACK == 1 and PLANES == 0:
        threadgroups (tiles(W, ceil_div(N, 64 / SERVED)), ceil_div(M, 64), 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (128, 1, 1)
    # An entry that ran one GEMV launch for every row count below
    # VERIFY_ROWS takes the `gemv` launch's tile mapping and lanes for the
    # other two (`restate single_gemv`); the launches' own defaults are the
    # entries that ran a launch per row class.
    mapping single_gemv:
        restate gemv_rows SIMDGROUPS in [16, 8, 4, 2, 32] default 16
        restate gemv_rows ROWS in [1, 2, 4] default 1
        restate gemv_pair SIMDGROUPS in [16, 8, 4, 2, 32] default 16
        restate gemv_pair ROWS in [1, 2, 4] default 1

# CUDA: the K1 projection library (`cuda/common/projection.cuh`). Every K1
# CUDA entry runs the GEMV to 16 rows and the GEMM beyond, in two row bands.
# The GEMV is the 16-bit path (the A-rounded activation in bf16/f16 MMAs
# against exact codes, rows independent of the row count), or with INT8 = 1
# the INT8 path the GEMMs take (int8_rule activations, the weights' s8 codes,
# one s8 MMA per 32 codes folded per group in k order, rows likewise
# independent of the row count): `gemv` to 8 rows, `gemv16` (two 8-row
# column blocks) from 9 to 16; 8 warps per block in groups of KSPLIT that
# split K and reduce in part order. The small-band GEMM
# (`gemm_small`, 17 to 64 rows: 64-row block tiles, 3 cp.async stages) has
# two operand paths: the 16-bit path (weights dequantized to A) and the INT8
# candidate (arithmetic INT8 = 1: activations quantized per 32 codes as q8_1
# does, s8 MMAs), which `where` admits only for weights the int8 GEMM takes
# (`form(W, INT8)`); the tuner keeps INT8 only where it is faster within
# tolerance. The large-band GEMM (`gemm`, beyond 64 rows: 128-row block
# tiles, 2 stages) is the 16-bit path; each stage's copies are issued by one
# of ROTATE rotating warp sets (the launch parameter ROTATE, tuned: its best
# value depends on the weight representation, and the arithmetic does not,
# so every value gives the same bits; likewise in the `gemm` launches of
# `attention`, `recurrent`, `readout` and `draft`). BLOCKS (the launch
# parameter, tuned; same bits at every value) is the large band's blocks an
# SM: 2 halves its registers (128 a thread) and declares the int8 GEMM's own
# layout bound (`form(W, INT8_SHARED)`) as its shared bytes, admitted for the
# int8 GEMM of single or segmented weights whose bound fits half an SM's
# shared memory (HALF_SM_SHARED: 100 KB an SM on sm_86 and sm_89, less 1 KB
# reserved a block). Its loop stalls with 8 warps an SM: on an RTX 3090 at
# 512 rows a third stage was no faster, and 2 blocks cut the int8 GEMM of
# q4g32s 13%, q8g32s and q3k 1% (runs 30053d, a8dd9f), while weights
# whose GEMM spills at 128 registers (q4k, q6k, q2k, the iq formats: 200 to
# 380 stack bytes) run 1.1 to 3.6x slower at 2; 1 is first, the smaller
# worst-case gap. Entries with few output
# columns split either band over K up to 128 rows (grid z: 2 shares of
# partials that `finalize` sums in part order). Measured on GB10 (17 to 512
# rows, both paths, split 1/2/4, tiles 32/64/128): up to 64 rows want the
# 64-row tiles, beyond them the 128-row ones, the few-column entries the
# split up to 128 rows. Staging launches form the rows a launch does not
# read in place: `stage` a normalized input's A rows (at one row the GEMV
# block forms its row in its shared memory instead), the shared operand
# stage the INT8 path's q8_1 rows plus (d, d * sum q) groups, for both bands
# past one row. At one row every GEMV block (an unordered segment's of an
# ordered entry and a part's included) forms its row in its shared memory,
# whatever its kind, with the operand sums its biased weights fold
# (`shared_row`, K * SHARED_ROW_PAIR_BYTES / 2 bytes of K / P: the B
# fragments are unconditional shared reads, and the sums are formed once a
# block, not once a k-block in every warp), or with INT8 = 1 its q8_1 row and
# groups (`shared_s8_row`, K * 5 / 4 bytes of the same region).

# The dynamic shared memory of a one-row CUDA GEMV block's row
# (`shared_row`), a byte count per two of its K columns: their two A
# elements (4 bytes), and their part of two areas of one F32 operand sum per
# 16 columns (1 byte). Every launch that can run a one-row block declares
# K * SHARED_ROW_PAIR_BYTES / 2 bytes where it runs one (dense's `gemv` and
# mixed `ordered_gemv`, routed's `choice`, `summed` and the shared expert's
# `gathered`), and the block traps on less (`require_dynamic_shared`), which
# also holds the kernels to this layout.
const SHARED_ROW_PAIR_BYTES = 5

# The forms below are the `dense` projection (`cuda/lib/projection/operator.cuh`,
# over the K1 library `cuda/lib/projection/projection.cuh`), `single` and
# `paired`, over rows of the kind its `project` line names. `rms` rows are
# formed by the entry's prologue (it normalizes them), so the stage launch
# materializes them only for more than one row; `staged` rows are formed by
# the stage launch alone, at every row count; `plain` rows are read in place
# unless a weight takes NVFP4 operands (`operands(W)`) or a matrix band takes
# the INT8 or OPERAND operands (INT8 in the GEMV band too). The one-row GEMV
# block reads every kind from the row it forms in its shared memory (above).
# KSPLIT splits K in each GEMV launch, a setting of each, defaulting to 4; an entry whose rows
# of the band all keep their one-row bits shares one KSPLIT between the two
# launches by restating it entry-wide (dense_up, dense_output). SPLIT (single) is the GEMM's split over
# K into shares up to 128 rows (grid z = 1 + min(1, 128 / M)), summed by
# `finalize`; it defaults to 2 where an entry always split (attention_output,
# dense_output, project_rows); dense_up, readout_head_rows, per_layer_gate and
# stream_mix_up sum whole sums and restate their own default of 1. The
# paired epilogue reads whole sums, so a pair does not split.
# The decoder-type forms (fold, records, INT8_LOCAL) reach every entry
# through `PACKETS_DECODER`.
# Parts (`parts P`, segmented): the GEMVs split K by part, P times the
# tiles, each block a part's (`gemv_parts`), a one-row block forming only its
# part's row, into F32 `partials` the last block to arrive (`arrivals`) adds
# in part order; the stage and the GEMMs read whole rows.
# A plane set (`PLANES`, a progressive head's planes; `readout.seismic`)
# takes one form, `planes` (`cuda/lib/projection/planes.cuh`): ROWS
# vocabulary rows a warp, WARPS warps a block, each block over 8 rows of
# the staged rows (grid y), lane l reading group l of each 1,024-column
# chunk of them, staged in shared memory once a block. The entry gives the
# view its rows are projected onto (the exact codes, or the 4-bit view with
# its rows' group sums), the epilogue and the rows' formation: the stage
# launch forms them at every row count, into `staged`, with whatever the
# view and epilogue read of them beside. Every other form, with its
# scratch, is gated off a plane set.
# STAGING 1 stages a single or segmented weight's block coefficients in
# shared memory, K-sized, in the GEMV launches; a pair's are read from device
# memory, and a parted entry's blocks, a part each, stage none (nor do its
# GEMMs take the INT8 or OPERAND operands). The GEMV launches' residency is
# the entry's own, restated where it ran it:
# RESIDENCY 0 leaves the 1..8-row GEMV's grid unstated, its blocks sharing an
# SM as registers allow, and RESIDENCY 1 or 2 states it, sharing an SM among
# up to that many of its blocks (dense_up and dense_output ran 1, tuned over
# 1 and 2, and restate it). Launch bounds are (256, 1) where nothing is stated.
projection dense for cuda:
    let ORDERED_ANY = min(1, sum(W, ORDERED))
    let ORDERED_ALL = sum(W, ORDERED) / WEIGHTS
    let ORDERED_GEMV_SHARED = 256 + max(2, M) * 1024
    let ZSPLIT = 1 for paired | segmented
    let ZSPLIT = 1 + (SPLIT - 1) * min(1, 128 / M) for single
    let OPERANDS = min(1, sum(W, operands(W)))
    let HALF_SM_SHARED = 49152
    params (arithmetic INT8 in [0, 1] default 0, arithmetic OPERAND in [0, 1] default 0,
        arithmetic SPLIT in [2, 1] default 2 for single,
        TPW in [1, 2] default 1 for ordered,
        form STAGING in [0, 1] default 0 for single | segmented, form STAGING in [0] default 0 for paired,
        arithmetic KSPLIT in [4, 2, 8, 1] default (4 - 3 * ORDERED_ANY))
    where dense_bytes(A) == 2
    where (ORDERED_ANY == 1 or KSPLIT != 1)
    where (ORDERED_ANY == 0 or (INT8 == 0 and OPERAND == 0 and STAGING == 0 and KSPLIT != 8))
    where (ORDERED_ANY == 0 or SPLIT == 2) for single
    where (ORDERED_ALL == 0 or TPW == 1) for ordered
    where (ORDERED_ALL == 0 or KSPLIT == 1)
    where (PLANES == 1 or K % 64 == 0 or (ORDERED_ALL == 1 and each(W, dense_bytes(W) > 0) and K % 32 == 0))
    where (OPERAND == 0 or (INT8 == 0 and PARTED == 0))
    where (INT8 == 0 or each(W, form(W, INT8) == 1)) for paired | single
    where (INT8 == 0 or (PARTED == 0 and each(W, N == 0 or form(W, INT8) == 1))) for segmented
    where (BLOCKS == 1 or (INT8 == 1 and each(W, N == 0 or form(W, INT8_SHARED) <= HALF_SM_SHARED))) for single | segmented
    where BLOCKS == 1 for paired
    where (STAGING == 0 or PARTED == 0)
    where (RESIDENCY != 2 or each(W, form(W, GEMV_RECORDS) == 0)) for paired | single
    where (G == 1 or (N % 16 == 0 and INT8 == 0 and OPERAND == 0 and each(W, operands(W) == 0))) for single
    scratch staged bytes (M * K * 2) when ORDERED_ALL == 1 and PUBLISHED == 0 and M > VERIFY_ROWS for rms
    scratch staged bytes (M * K * 2) when ORDERED_ANY == 1 and ORDERED_ALL == 0 and M > 1 for rms
    scratch staged bytes (M * K * 2) when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and PUBLISHED == 0 and (M > 1 or PLANES == 1) for rms
    scratch staged bytes (M * K * 2) when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and PUBLISHED == 0 for staged
    scratch staged bytes (M * K * max(1 + OPERAND, 2 * OPERANDS)) when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and ((M > 1 and (OPERANDS == 1 or INT8 == 1)) or (M > 16 and OPERAND == 1)) for plain
    scratch groups bytes (M * K / 4) when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and INT8 == 1 and M > 1 and PLANES == 0
    scratch partials bytes (SPLIT * G * M * N * 4) when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 16 and M <= 128 and SPLIT > 1 and PLANES == 0 for single
    scratch partials bytes (M * P * sum(W, N) * 4) when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M <= 16 and PARTED == 1 for segmented
    scratch arrivals bytes (4) sync when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M <= 16 and PARTED == 1 for segmented
    launch ordered_stage for rms when ORDERED_ALL == 1 and M > VERIFY_ROWS:
        staging
        threadgroups (M, 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
    launch ordered_stage for rms when ORDERED_ANY == 1 and ORDERED_ALL == 0 and M > 1:
        staging
        threadgroups (M, 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
    launch ordered_gemv when ORDERED_ALL == 1 and M <= VERIFY_ROWS:
        threadgroups (tiles(W, ceil_div(N, 32)), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (ORDERED_GEMV_SHARED)
    launch ordered_gemv for segmented when ORDERED_ANY == 1 and ORDERED_ALL == 0 and M <= VERIFY_ROWS:
        threadgroups (tiles(W, ORDERED * ceil_div(N, 32) + (1 - ORDERED) * ceil_div(ceil_div(N, 16 * TPW), 8 / KSPLIT)), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (max(ORDERED_GEMV_SHARED, (1 - min(1, M - 1)) * K * SHARED_ROW_PAIR_BYTES / 2))
    launch ordered_gemm when ORDERED_ALL == 1 and M > VERIFY_ROWS:
        threadgroups (tiles(W, ceil_div(N, 32)), ceil_div(M, 64), G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (9216)
    launch stage for rms when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 1 and PLANES == 0:
        reads (INT8, OPERAND)
        staging
        threadgroups (M, 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
    launch stage for rms when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and PLANES == 1:
        threadgroups (M, 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
    launch stage for staged when ORDERED_ANY == 0:
        reads (INT8, OPERAND)
        staging
        threadgroups (M, 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
    launch stage for plain when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and ((M > 1 and (OPERANDS == 1 or INT8 == 1)) or (M > 16 and OPERAND == 1)):
        reads (INT8, OPERAND)
        staging
        threadgroups (M, 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
    launch gemv when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M <= 8 and PLANES == 0:
        params (RESIDENCY in [0, 1, 2] default 0 for paired | single)
        reads (INT8, STAGING)
        threadgroups (P * tiles(W, ceil_div(ceil_div(N, 16), 8 / KSPLIT)), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes ((1 - min(1, M - 1)) * (K / P) * SHARED_ROW_PAIR_BYTES / 2)
    launch gemv16 when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 8 and M <= 16 and PLANES == 0:
        reads (INT8, STAGING)
        alike (gemv)
        threadgroups (P * tiles(W, ceil_div(ceil_div(N, 16), 8 / KSPLIT)), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
    launch gemm_small when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 16 and M <= 64 and PLANES == 0:
        reads (INT8, OPERAND)
        threadgroups (tiles(W, ceil_div(ceil_div(N, 16), 8)), 1, ZSPLIT * G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (3 * (64 * 144 + SERVED * 10240) + SERVED * 2048)
    launch gemm when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 64 and PLANES == 0:
        params (ROTATE in [2, 1, 4] default 2, BLOCKS in [1, 2] default 1)
        reads (INT8, OPERAND)
        threadgroups (tiles(W, ceil_div(ceil_div(N, 16), 8)), ceil_div(M, 128), ZSPLIT * G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes ((2 - BLOCKS) * (2 * (128 * 144 + SERVED * 10240) + SERVED * 2048) + (BLOCKS - 1) * most(W, form(W, INT8_SHARED)))
    launch finalize for single when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > 16 and M <= 128 and SPLIT > 1 and PLANES == 0:
        reads (SPLIT)
        threadgroups (ceil_div(M * N, 256), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
    launch planes for single when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and PLANES == 1:
        params (WARPS in [8, 4, 2] default 8, ROWS in [2, 1, 4] default 2)
        threadgroups (ceil_div(N, WARPS * ROWS), ceil_div(M, 8), 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (WARPS * 32, 1, 1)

# Vulkan: the K1 projection library (`vulkan/lib/projection/projection.glsl`)
# as the `dense` projection (`vulkan/lib/projection/operator.glsl`). Rows to
# 8 run the GEMV (SIMDGROUPS x ROWS lane groups of LANES lanes a workgroup,
# each owning weight rows; LANES sets the reduction order, so it is
# arithmetic), as one launch per activation-row bound (`gemv1`, `gemv2`,
# `gemv4` for 3-4 rows, `gemv8` for 5-8): one bound per pipeline, since the
# driver's pipeline creation is superlinear in the unrolled body. Past 8 rows
# the GEMM over TILE_M x TILE_N tiles of SUB_M x SUB_N subgroup tiles
# (cooperative-matrix f16 multiplies under SEISMIC_HAS_MATRIX, F32 FMAs
# otherwise), a pair's tile taking TILE_N / 2 features of each weight; a
# single projection's GEMM may split K SPLIT ways into partials `finalize`
# sums in part order. The rows are of the `project` line's kind, as on CUDA:
# `rms` rows the GEMV normalizes while staging them and the stage launch
# forms past 8 rows; `staged` rows the stage launch alone forms (its body the
# entry's), at every row count; `plain` rows are read in place unless a
# weight takes NVFP4 operands (`operands(W)`), which the GEMV forms while
# staging and the stage launch past 8 rows. The GEMV's shared region holds the
# rows' squares, the NVFP4 operands' global scales and the staged packets
# (`projection.glsl`). Every launch that decodes the weights holds its own
# region rounded to 8 bytes and, where every device holds that region with
# them (its footprint, the 16-byte views' largest, within the backend's
# floor, FLOOR_SHARED_BYTES), their grids' and codebooks' tables (their
# `form(W, TABLE)` bytes, rounded to 8) and a 4-byte pad: the region's u32 length
# is then odd, and odd only then, which is how the library tells it stages
# the tables there once a workgroup (`packets_stage_tables`) rather than
# reading them in place. Every weight is one the packet decoder reads
# (`form(W, DECODED)`, `vulkan/producers.decl`). Groups: every launch but the stage runs group g at
# grid z (z = g * SPLIT + part in the GEMM), over the group's columns, weight
# rows and output columns, and its own G-th of the split partials; the
# NVFP4-operand form stages the whole row and runs only G = 1.
# Parts (`parts P`, segmented): each GEMV workgroup serves one part's row
# tile over that part's own rows (`projection_parts_gemv`), P times the
# tiles, into F32 `partials` that `combine` adds in part order; the stage
# launch normalizes a row's parts, one workgroup each, for the GEMM.
projection dense for vulkan:
    let ORDERED_ANY = min(1, sum(W, ORDERED))
    let ORDERED_ALL = sum(W, ORDERED) / WEIGHTS
    let OPERANDS = min(1, sum(W, operands(W)))
    let GEMV_SHARED = 256 + 32 * OPERANDS + min(8 * ceil_div(K / P, 32), 288) * 72
    let TABLE_SUM = sum(W, form(W, TABLE))
    let TABLE_REGION = min(1, TABLE_SUM) * (8 * ceil_div(TABLE_SUM, 8) + 4)
    let GEMV_REGION = 8 * ceil_div(GEMV_SHARED, 8)
    let GEMV_HELD = GEMV_REGION + TABLE_REGION * (1 - min(1, 16 * ceil_div(GEMV_REGION + TABLE_REGION, 16) / (FLOOR_SHARED_BYTES + 1)))
    let GEMM_REGION = (TILE_M + TILE_N) * 80
    let GEMM_HELD = GEMM_REGION + TABLE_REGION * (1 - min(1, 16 * ceil_div(GEMM_REGION + TABLE_REGION, 16) / (FLOOR_SHARED_BYTES + 1)))
    let ORDERED_GEMV_REGION = 8448
    let ORDERED_GEMV_HELD = ORDERED_GEMV_REGION + TABLE_REGION * (1 - min(1, 16 * ceil_div(ORDERED_GEMV_REGION + TABLE_REGION, 16) / (FLOOR_SHARED_BYTES + 1)))
    let ORDERED_GEMM_REGION = 9216
    let ORDERED_GEMM_HELD = ORDERED_GEMM_REGION + TABLE_REGION * (1 - min(1, 16 * ceil_div(ORDERED_GEMM_REGION + TABLE_REGION, 16) / (FLOOR_SHARED_BYTES + 1)))
    let MIXED_GEMV1_REGION = 8 * ceil_div(max(2304, GEMV_SHARED), 8)
    let MIXED_GEMV1_HELD = MIXED_GEMV1_REGION + TABLE_REGION * (1 - min(1, 16 * ceil_div(MIXED_GEMV1_REGION + TABLE_REGION, 16) / (FLOOR_SHARED_BYTES + 1)))
    let MIXED_GEMV4_REGION = 8 * ceil_div(max(4352, GEMV_SHARED), 8)
    let MIXED_GEMV4_HELD = MIXED_GEMV4_REGION + TABLE_REGION * (1 - min(1, 16 * ceil_div(MIXED_GEMV4_REGION + TABLE_REGION, 16) / (FLOOR_SHARED_BYTES + 1)))
    let MIXED_GEMV8_REGION = 8 * ceil_div(max(8448, GEMV_SHARED), 8)
    let MIXED_GEMV8_HELD = MIXED_GEMV8_REGION + TABLE_REGION * (1 - min(1, 16 * ceil_div(MIXED_GEMV8_REGION + TABLE_REGION, 16) / (FLOOR_SHARED_BYTES + 1)))
    let SPLITS = 1 for paired | segmented
    let SPLITS = SPLIT for single
    params (SIMDGROUPS in [16, 8, 4, 2, 32] default (16 - 8 * ORDERED_ANY), ROWS in [1, 2, 4] default 1, arithmetic LANES in [16, 32] default (16 + 16 * ORDERED_ANY * (1 - ORDERED_ALL)),
        TILE_M in [128, 64, 32] default 64, TILE_N in [128, 64] default 128, SUB_M in [32, 64] default 32, SUB_N in [32, 64] default 32,
        arithmetic SPLIT in [1, 2, 4] default 1 for single)
    where dense_bytes(A) == 2
    where (ORDERED_ANY == 0 or SIMDGROUPS <= 16)
    where (ORDERED_ANY == 0 or (TILE_M == 64 and TILE_N == 128 and SUB_M == 32 and SUB_N == 32))
    where (ORDERED_ANY == 0 or SPLIT == 1) for single
    where (ORDERED_ALL == 0 or (ROWS == 1 and LANES == 16))
    where SUB_M <= TILE_M and SUB_N <= TILE_N
    where (G == 1 or OPERANDS == 0)
    where each(W, form(W, DECODED) == 1)
    scratch partials bytes (SPLIT * G * M * N * 4) when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > VERIFY_ROWS and SPLIT > 1 for single
    scratch partials bytes (M * P * sum(W, N) * 4) when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M <= VERIFY_ROWS and PARTED == 1 for segmented
    scratch staged bytes (M * K * 2) when ORDERED_ALL == 1 and PUBLISHED == 0 and M > VERIFY_ROWS for rms
    scratch staged bytes (M * K * 2) when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and PUBLISHED == 0 and M > VERIFY_ROWS for rms
    scratch staged bytes (M * K * 2) when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and PUBLISHED == 0 for staged
    scratch staged bytes (M * K * 2) when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > VERIFY_ROWS and OPERANDS == 1 for plain
    launch ordered_stage for rms when ORDERED_ALL == 1 and M > VERIFY_ROWS:
        staging
        threadgroups (M, 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (2064)
    launch ordered_gemv when ORDERED_ALL == 1 and M <= VERIFY_ROWS:
        threadgroups (tiles(W, ceil_div(N, 4 * SIMDGROUPS)), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (SIMDGROUPS * 32, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (ORDERED_GEMV_HELD)
    launch ordered_gemv1 for segmented when ORDERED_ANY == 1 and ORDERED_ALL == 0 and M <= 1:
        threadgroups (tiles(W, ORDERED * ceil_div(N, 4 * SIMDGROUPS) + (1 - ORDERED) * ceil_div(N, SIMDGROUPS * ROWS * 32 / LANES)), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (SIMDGROUPS * 32, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (MIXED_GEMV1_HELD)
    launch ordered_gemv2 for segmented when ORDERED_ANY == 1 and ORDERED_ALL == 0 and M == 2:
        alike (ordered_gemv1)
        threadgroups (tiles(W, ORDERED * ceil_div(N, 4 * SIMDGROUPS) + (1 - ORDERED) * ceil_div(N, SIMDGROUPS * ROWS * 32 / LANES)), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (SIMDGROUPS * 32, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (MIXED_GEMV1_HELD)
    launch ordered_gemv4 for segmented when ORDERED_ANY == 1 and ORDERED_ALL == 0 and M >= 3 and M <= 4:
        alike (ordered_gemv1)
        threadgroups (tiles(W, ORDERED * ceil_div(N, 4 * SIMDGROUPS) + (1 - ORDERED) * ceil_div(N, SIMDGROUPS * ROWS * 32 / LANES)), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (SIMDGROUPS * 32, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (MIXED_GEMV4_HELD)
    launch ordered_gemv8 for segmented when ORDERED_ANY == 1 and ORDERED_ALL == 0 and M >= 5 and M <= VERIFY_ROWS:
        alike (ordered_gemv1)
        threadgroups (tiles(W, ORDERED * ceil_div(N, 4 * SIMDGROUPS) + (1 - ORDERED) * ceil_div(N, SIMDGROUPS * ROWS * 32 / LANES)), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (SIMDGROUPS * 32, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (MIXED_GEMV8_HELD)
    launch ordered_gemm when ORDERED_ALL == 1 and M > VERIFY_ROWS:
        threadgroups (tiles(W, ceil_div(N, 32)), ceil_div(M, 64), G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (ORDERED_GEMM_HELD)
    launch stage for rms when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > VERIFY_ROWS:
        staging
        threadgroups (M * P, 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (128)
    launch stage for staged when ORDERED_ANY == 0:
        staging
        threadgroups (M, 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (128 * OPERANDS)
    launch stage for plain when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > VERIFY_ROWS and OPERANDS == 1:
        staging
        threadgroups (M, 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (128)
    launch gemv1 when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M <= 1:
        threadgroups (P * tiles(W, ceil_div(N, SIMDGROUPS * ROWS * 32 / LANES)), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (SIMDGROUPS * 32, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (GEMV_HELD)
    launch gemv2 when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M == 2:
        alike (gemv1)
        threadgroups (P * tiles(W, ceil_div(N, SIMDGROUPS * ROWS * 32 / LANES)), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (SIMDGROUPS * 32, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (GEMV_HELD)
    launch gemv4 when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M >= 3 and M <= 4:
        alike (gemv1)
        threadgroups (P * tiles(W, ceil_div(N, SIMDGROUPS * ROWS * 32 / LANES)), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (SIMDGROUPS * 32, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (GEMV_HELD)
    launch gemv8 when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M >= 5 and M <= VERIFY_ROWS:
        alike (gemv1)
        threadgroups (P * tiles(W, ceil_div(N, SIMDGROUPS * ROWS * 32 / LANES)), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (SIMDGROUPS * 32, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (GEMV_HELD)
    launch combine for segmented when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M <= VERIFY_ROWS and PARTED == 1:
        threadgroups (ceil_div(M * sum(W, N), 256), 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
    launch gemm when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > VERIFY_ROWS:
        threadgroups (tiles(W, ceil_div(N, TILE_N / SERVED)), ceil_div(M, TILE_M), SPLITS * G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (TILE_M * TILE_N * 32 / (SUB_M * SUB_N), 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (GEMM_HELD)
    launch finalize for single when ORDERED_ANY == 0 and M > VERIFY_ROWS and SPLIT > 1:
        threadgroups (ceil_div(M * N, 256), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)

# CPU: the CPU projection library (`cpu/lib/projection/projection.rs`).
# INT8 is a form on every CPU projection, as on Metal: INT8 = 1 quantizes
# the staged rows to Q8 blocks and runs the representation's integer dot
# (VNNI or AVX2 products, NEON SDOT, eight-row tiles over four activation
# rows), a different algorithm from the F32 dot whose best ROWS and
# participant counts say nothing about the F32 form's. `where` admits it
# where a weight it multiplies takes the quantized dot (`form(W, INT8)`:
# floating dense weights and packed weights but those whose products take
# NVFP4 operand rows, which multiply the rows their recipe forms). As a form its one
# representative is measured right after the defaults, before any F32
# refinement. As a plain parameter it came after the three ROWS moves:
# gemma-4-e2b QAT Q4 on an EPYC 9V45 (8 cores, 60 s) measured only its
# default for dense_expand (43% of the objective), and project_rows reached
# INT8 sixth, at 16 us against the F32 form's 278 us per decode row.

# The CPU projection operator (`projection quantized for cpu`): an entry
# takes it with `project quantized VARIANT (W, ..) over (ROWS, WIDTH)`,
# naming the element parameters of the weights it multiplies and the
# activation rows (`M`) and their width (`K`) it quantizes, in `G`
# independent groups of rows where it names them (`groups G`, else one). It
# owns what every entry restated: the
# tuned `ROWS` block and the INT8 form, admitted where a weight takes the
# quantized dot (`form(W, INT8)`), and the Q8 blocks' scratch, in tiles of
# `Q8_ROWS` rows (`tiled`, the tile kernel's) or each row alone (`rows`).
# A weight that multiplies rows of its own (`W over (ROWS, WIDTH)`: a
# product the entry forms between two projections, or an operand of rows
# its own) has its own buffers of them, each row alone (`<stem>_quantized`),
# and the others share `quantized`, so one line mixes them (`rows (GW, UW,
# DW over (T, F)) over (M, H)`). The sixteen-row block (`ROWS = 16`) is
# one AMX tile pair (`form(W, INT8_AMX)`, the VNNI tier running a row range
# below it or its tail in the same call), so it is offered with the INT8
# form where a weight takes the AMX tiles. The staging, quantizing and dot
# are `cpu/lib/projection`'s. An entry whose dot is its own
# takes none of it: its rows are split by the pool (`device.units`), and as a
# producer it names only its `emits` line.
#
# A consumer's activation operand is the operator's too, formed once. The
# entry names where each operand's rows come from, the entry's rows first,
# then each weight's own (`operand (SOURCE [tiles (COND)], ..)`, its Q8
# blocks a `tiled` projection's tiles only where `COND` holds): a tensor
# parameter (`PARAMETER [at (INDEX)] [within (FIRST, COUNT)] [normed
# (WEIGHT, EPSILON)]`: each row the row `INDEX` names where it names one,
# only rows `FIRST[0]` to `FIRST[0] + COUNT[0]` where it has a window,
# formed under the norm where it has one), the entry's function of a row
# (`values (FUNCTION)`), or a weight's own rows that the entry's launch
# stores and forms in its epilogue (`emitted`, `projection::emit`;
# `EMITTED`). The operand's forms are these buffers, the k-th of each the
# k-th operand's: its Q8 blocks (`operand`, written where `formed` holds:
# `INT8 == 1`) and its formed F32 rows (`operand rows`: what its exact
# products read, NVFP4 operand rows where every weight takes them; where
# only some of the weights of the entry's rows do, their NVFP4 copy follows
# the rows). The `form` launch (`<entry>_form`, its body generated from the
# declaration's formation) forms every operand but an emitted one: one work
# item a part of a row of every operand's rows in turn,
# `ceil_div(FORM_WIDTH, Q8_VALUES * FORM_ROWS)` parts of whole Q8 blocks a
# row, so a launch of few rows spreads a row over the pool; every part
# reduces the RMS factor over the whole row in one order and decodes only
# its own columns of the norm, and a row taken as NVFP4 operands, whose
# scale spans it, or an entry function's row, is formed whole by its first
# part. No entry writes a stage launch.
#
# A producer names the results whose operands its launches write (`emits
# (result N over (ROWS, WIDTH) [normed (WEIGHT, EPSILON)], ..)`; `project
# quantized emits (..)` alone takes nothing else): each emitted result gets
# the `for emits` buffers over its rows and width, named `result_N_<name>`:
# its rows, their Q8 blocks and one arrival counter a row
# (`projection::emit`: the row's last arrival forms the rows from the whole
# stored row as the formation does, `form_input` under the norm else the
# stored values staged, quantizes them, then applies the NVFP4 transform).
# A graph places a consumer's operand where its tensor's producer emits it
# under the same norm weight and epsilon, when sealed, and leaves the
# consumer's `form` launch out where every form it writes is so placed and
# its `operand when` holds (tiles are a layout of their own, so `tiled`
# pairs one row alone; an operand gathered `at` rows, or under an unbound
# norm, never pairs). The seal sets the producer's word of each emitted
# buffer from the consumer's forms (`emits_result_N_<name>()`, and on the
# rows `nvfp4_result_N_rows()`), and the producer writes them only under it.
# Elsewhere, a standalone call among them, the `form` launch forms the
# operand, and the producer's only emission work is reading the words.
projection quantized for cpu:
    let FORM_ROWS = G * M + sum(W, (OWN - EMITTED) * M) for tiled | rows
    let FORM_WIDTH = most(W, (1 - EMITTED) * K) for tiled | rows
    let SHARED = sum(W, 1 - OWN) for tiled | rows
    let RECIPES = sum(W, (1 - OWN) * operands(W)) for tiled | rows
    params (ROWS in [8, 16, 4, 2, 1] default 8, arithmetic form INT8 in [0, 1] default 0 for tiled | rows)
    where (INT8 == 0 or any(W, form(W, INT8) == 1)) for tiled | rows
    where (ROWS < 16 or (INT8 == 1 and any(W, form(W, INT8_AMX) == 1))) for tiled | rows
    scratch quantized bytes (G * ceil_div(M, Q8_ROWS) * Q8_ROWS * ceil_div(K, Q8_VALUES) * Q8_BYTES) operand when (G * M == 1) formed (INT8 == 1) for tiled
    scratch quantized bytes (M * ceil_div(K, Q8_VALUES) * Q8_BYTES) operand formed (INT8 == 1) for rows
    scratch rows bytes (G * M * K * 4 * (1 + min(1, min(RECIPES, SHARED - RECIPES)))) operand rows when (RECIPES == 0 or RECIPES == SHARED) nvfp4 (RECIPES == SHARED) for tiled | rows
    scratch quantized bytes (M * ceil_div(K, Q8_VALUES) * Q8_BYTES) operand for emits
    scratch rows bytes (M * K * 4) operand rows for emits
    scratch arrivals bytes (M * 4) sync for emits
    each W:
        scratch quantized bytes (M * ceil_div(K, Q8_VALUES) * Q8_BYTES) operand formed (INT8 == 1) for tiled | rows
        scratch rows bytes (M * K * 4) operand rows nvfp4 (operands(W) == 1) for tiled | rows
    launch form for tiled | rows:
        staging
        threadgroups (FORM_ROWS, ceil_div(FORM_WIDTH, Q8_VALUES * FORM_ROWS), 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (1, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (FORM_WIDTH * 4)

# A plain projection of A rows, published in Y: F32 where a row op consumes
# the projection before the residual (`post_norm_residual`'s projected rows:
# attention and feed-forward outputs of post-norm blocks, the per-layer
# input's projection back to the hidden width), A where it feeds another
# projection (Nemotron's latent down).
#
# A block-diagonal weight of G groups: each row's columns split into G
# consecutive runs of K, and run g projects through its own block of N
# weight rows, `weight[g * N : (g + 1) * N]`, into output columns
# g * N .. (g + 1) * N (DeepSeek V4.1's grouped attention output). The
# ungrouped projection is G = 1. One scale and bound cover the whole tensor.
fn project_rows[M, G, K, N, WS, WB](source: &tensor[M, G * K] A, weight: &tensor[G * N, K] W,
    weight_scale: &tensor[WS] f32, weight_bound: &tensor[WB] f32) -> tensor[M, G * N] Y
    where G >= 1 and WS >= 0 and WS <= 1 and WB >= 0 and (WB == 0 or K % WB == 0):
    # The rows are dense activations: staging them in A (an exact copy)
    # states that domain, which the CUDA forms' A staging requires.
    let mut rows = tensor[M, G * K] A
    parallel for row in 0..M:
        rows[row] = source[row]
    let mut sum = tensor[M, G * N] f32
    let mut result = tensor[M, G * N] Y
    for group in 0..G:
        linear(rows[:, group * K : (group + 1) * K], weight[group * N : (group + 1) * N],
            sum[:, group * N : (group + 1) * N])
    scale_rows(sum, weight_scale, result)
    return result

# Metal: the `dense` projection, single, over the source rows and the groups
# of a grouped weight; the NVFP4 operands of a weight that takes them are the
# entry's own prologue (`stage`, into `staged`, G = 1 only).
native project_rows for metal from "metal/project_rows.metal":
    static (G, K, N, WS, WB)
    where WS <= 1
    project dense single (weight) groups G
    scratch staged bytes (M * K * 2) when M > VERIFY_ROWS and operands(W) == 1
    launch project_rows_stage before batch when M > VERIFY_ROWS and operands(W) == 1:
        staging
        threadgroups (M, 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)

# Vulkan: the `dense` projection (single) over the source rows and the groups
# of a grouped weight, as on CUDA.
native project_rows for vulkan from "vulkan/project_rows.comp":
    static (G, K, N, WS)
    where WS <= 1
    project dense single (weight) groups G

# `attention_output`'s bands (GEMV to 16 rows reading the rows in place, the
# INT8 candidate on either matrix band, split-K to 128 rows) with a store
# epilogue in Y.
#
# Groups: every launch but the stage runs group g at grid z (z = g in the
# GEMV and finalize launches, z = g * split + part in the GEMMs), over the
# group's source columns, weight rows and output columns, and its own G-th
# of the split partials. A group's weight rows start on a whole 16-row tile
# (N % 16 == 0). The staged forms (INT8, OPERAND, NVFP4 operands) stage the
# whole source row and run only G = 1.
native project_rows for cuda from "cuda/project_rows.cu":
    static (G, K, N, WS)
    where WS <= 1
    project dense single (weight) groups G

# Groups: the operator's `form` launch forms each row's G runs of K as G
# operand rows (group-major), and the row launch's work item (item, group)
# projects the group's ROWS weight rows against its operand rows.
native project_rows for cpu from "cpu/project_rows.rs":
    static (WS)
    where WS <= 1
    project quantized tiled (W) over (M, K) groups G operand (source)
    launch project_rows_rows:
        threadgroups (ceil_div(N, ROWS), G, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (1, 1, 1)
